  "solution_principle": "10- Surface Transformation: Division, Offset, Flip, Join, etc...\r\n\r\n- Surfaces can be transformed by many components with various results.\r\nTry the following components and check their INPUTS in order to use them:\r\n- \"Divide Surface\"\r\n- \"Isotrim\"\r\n- \"Offset\"\r\n- \"Brep Join\"\r\n\r\n- To join two surfaces together, we need to use the \"Brep Join\" component. There is not a \"Surface Join\" component in Grasshopper since surfaces are also considered as Breps.\r\nA surface is an \"open\" Brep.\r\nAn \"open\" Brep can also be made out of many surfaces joined together, but not forming a closed solid.\r\nA \"closed\" Brep is essentially a closed solid object.",
